<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Verchen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1164</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Verchen was fought on 6 July 1164 near Demmin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>, where an army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-i-of-denmark">Valdemar I of Denmark</a>, defeated the Pomeranian dukes Bogislaw I and Casimir I and the Obotrite prince Pribislav. The defeat forced the Pomeranian dukes to submit to Henry the Lion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-verchen.jpg" alt="Battle of Verchen" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LordFarrow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vorwall.slawische.Burganlage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
